1
00:04:28,571 --> 00:04:34,571
What killed the dinosaurs?

2
00:08:57,142 --> 00:09:03,142
Ice Age: Dawn of the Dinosaurs is a animation, comedy,
family film directed by Carlos Saldanha.

3
00:13:25,714 --> 00:13:31,714
Times are changing for Manny the moody mammoth, Sid the motor
mouthed sloth and Diego the crafty saber-toothed tiger.

4
00:17:54,285 --> 00:18:00,285
Life heats up for our heroes when they meet some new and
none-too-friendly neighbors – the mighty dinosaurs.

5
00:22:22,857 --> 00:22:28,857
Manny (voice), played by Ray Romano.

6
00:26:51,428 --> 00:26:57,428
Sid (voice), played by John Leguizamo.

7
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Diego (voice), played by Denis Leary.

8
00:35:48,571 --> 00:35:54,571
Ellie (voice), played by Queen Latifah.

9
00:40:17,142 --> 00:40:23,142
Buck (voice), played by Simon Pegg.

10
00:44:45,714 --> 00:44:51,714
Crash (voice), played by Seann William Scott.

11
00:49:14,285 --> 00:49:20,285
Ice Age: Dawn of the Dinosaurs is a 2009 American animated
adventure comedy film produced by Blue Sky Studios.

12
00:53:42,857 --> 00:53:48,857
The third in the Ice Age film series, it was directed by Carlos Saldanha, and
written by Michael Berg, Peter Ackerman, Mike Reiss, and Yoni Brenner.

13
00:58:11,428 --> 00:58:17,428
John Leguizamo, Ray Romano and Denis Leary reprise their roles from the first two
films and Queen Latifah reprises her role from the second film.

14
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:46,000
In the film, while Manny and Ellie are preparing for their baby, Sid the Sloth is kidnapped by a female Tyrannosaurus after stealing
her eggs, leading the rest of the herd to rescue him in a tropical lost world inhabited by dinosaurs underneath the ice.

15
01:07:08,571 --> 01:07:14,571
Ice Age: Dawn of the Dinosaurs was released on July 1, 2009 by 20th Century Fox.

16
01:11:37,142 --> 01:11:43,142
It received mixed reviews from critics, with praise for
its animation but criticism for the story.

17
01:16:05,714 --> 01:16:11,714
The film grossed $887 million worldwide, becoming the
third-highest-grossing film and the highest-grossing animated film of 2009.

18
01:20:34,285 --> 01:20:40,285
It was followed by two further sequels, Ice Age: Continental
Drift in 2012 and Ice Age: Collision Course in 2016.

19
01:25:02,857 --> 01:25:08,857
The film explores themes of insanity, ice age, villain, bridge, sequel.

20
01:29:31,428 --> 01:29:37,428
The tone is lighthearted.
